course: dictionary
lesson: 7989
title: Recruit: finding people to join
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and context tells you which one is meant. The word recruit can be a verb (an action) or a noun (a person). «Older boys tried to recruit Jake» is an action: they wanted him to join their group.
explain: Look at the clues around the word. The boys called Jake «little bro» and bought him chips. Those are friendly things to do, so they are trying to make Jake feel special and want to join them. That tells you recruit means to get someone to join a group.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. «Older boys tried to find and get Jake to join them» still makes sense, so you have the right meaning. Once you know it, you can spot the same idea in «new recruits» and «recruitment».
fact: Recruit can be a verb or a noun, so check the sentence to see which one it is.
fact: As a verb, recruit means to find and get new people to join a group, team, army or company.
fact: As a noun, a recruit is a new member, especially of the army or police.
fact: «Recruitment» is the process of finding new people to join a group.
fact: If someone older buys you treats and asks you to join their group, tell a trusted adult.
exercise: «Older boys tried to recruit Jake.» What does recruit mean here? | *To get Jake to join their group | To buy Jake some chips | To teach Jake to run fast | To take a photo of Jake
exercise: «The army's new recruits began training on Monday.» What is a recruit? | Teachers who give out homework | Shops that sell sweets | Old machines that no longer work | *New members who have just joined
exercise: Mia says, «I recruited my brother to help me wash the car.» What does recruited mean? | Gave him a present | Sent him away | Hired a car washer | *Got someone to help you
test: «The club wants to recruit ten new volunteers.» What is the club trying to do? | Close down for good | Sell its old equipment | Hold a party for its members | *Find and get new people to join
test: Which sentence uses recruit as a noun? | We recruit new members each year | I recruited my dad to carry the bags | They will recruit more players next season | *She was the newest recruit in the police team
exam: Why might the older boys buy Jake chips and call him «little bro»? | Because chips are his favourite food and it is his birthday | To say sorry for a fight | To pay him back for a game they lost | *To make him feel special so he wants to join them
